<title>USA: Colonial BancGroup Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Colonial BancGroup Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MONTGOMERY, Ala. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Selected Financial Data</p>
<p>					 Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>					     1997	 1996   97 to 96</p>
<p>Net interest income</p>
<p>  (taxable equivalent)	    $53,983    $45,769	  18%</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses	  2,854	1,750	  63%</p>
<p> Noninterest income		  18,401     17,640	   4%</p>
<p> Noninterest expense		 42,662     39,812	   7%</p>
<p> Net income			    16,723     13,623	  23%</p>
<p>Average primary shares</p>
<p>  outstanding			  39,679     37,158</p>
<p>Average fully diluted</p>
<p>  shares outstanding		 40,279     37,908</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>  Primary				  0.42	 0.36	  17%</p>
<p>  Fully diluted			  0.42	 0.35	  20%</p>
<p>	   (Dollars in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Restated financial results above reflect the January, 1997 mergers of Colonial BancGroup with Jefferson Bancorp and D/W Bankshares. The mergers were accounted for as poolings of interests and the financial results restated accordingly, the company said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
